c3d27b5ac4.png)\n\n \n\nA point $(x,y,z)$ on the surface generated by rotating the graph of $y=f(x)$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis for $x\\in [a,b]$ has the position vector\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=⟨x,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,f(x)\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [a,b],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, notice that $y=f(x)=2{x}^{2}\\ge 0$ for all $x\\in [0,1].$\n\nSo, the parametrization of our surface of revolution is\n\n$$\nr(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ⟩,\\,x\\in [0,\\,1],\\,\\theta \\in [0,2\\pi ).\n$$" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387709 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387710 13194139536184 true] [17592186387709 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536184 true] [17592186387709 1041 "field-1" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387709 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387710 13194139536184 true] [17592186387709 1110 #uuid "9cd5645a-bb02-50d6-ab57-ba6efb60d440" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387710 1034 "2x^2\\sin(\\theta)" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387710 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536184 true] [17592186387710 1111 #uuid "2a1b278d-224b-5594-87d3-ffaf6c790e83" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387711 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387712 13194139536184 true] [17592186387711 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536184 true] [17592186387711 1041 "field-2" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387711 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387712 13194139536184 true] [17592186387711 1110 #uuid "69b628fd-2c59-5c95-a3de-296f16a04e92" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387712 1034 "1" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387712 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536184 true] [17592186387712 1111 #uuid "85cacb4f-f5f3-5362-8e77-2ab2605c3f4a" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387713 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387714 13194139536184 true] [17592186387713 1089 "q-167648" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387713 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536184 true] [17592186387713 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/matha