                                \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $R(0)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387725 1113 #uuid "baad2f93-c0ec-5c20-ad38-e702dee28594" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387725 1145 "In part 1, we found that the curvature of the curve at the point $x=0$ is\n\n$$\nκ(0)=4.\n$$\n\nAs a result, the radius of curvature is\n\n$$\nR(0)=\\frac{1}{κ(0)}=\\frac{1}{4}.\n$$" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387726 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387727 13194139536184 true] [17592186387726 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536184 true] [17592186387726 1041 "field-1" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387726 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387727 13194139536184 true] [17592186387726 1110 #uuid "204c7662-aef8-5780-b91d-86eee6d9a6f2" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387727 1034 "\\frac{1}{4}" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387727 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536184 true] [17592186387727 1111 #uuid "43e2d991-8d8a-5550-b925-39b56baaf019" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387728 1017 #edb/ref 17592186387729 13194139536184 true] [17592186387728 1089 "q-167658" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387728 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536184 true] [17592186387728 1100 "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14083460/assets/22a909d34b63517bf5ccf90560a8070d20e1aa91a6c9eaf8f4e5326208b9d751.png)\n\n \n\nThe shell above is obtained by rotating the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ for $x\\in [0,1]$ by $2\\pi $ radians about the $x$-axis, as shown above. For each point $(x,y,z)$ on the shell, the charge density (electric charge per unit surface area) of the shell is given by the function \n\n$$\nd(x,y,z)=\\frac{x({y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nEarlier part 1:\n\nFind the curvature $κ(x)$ of the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ at $x=0.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $κ(0)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $4$\n\nEarlier part 2:\n\nWhat is the radius of curvature $R(x)$ of the curve $y=2{x}^{2}$ at the point $x=0?$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $R(0)=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $\\frac{1}{4}$\n\nEarlier part 3:\n\nWrite down the integral that gives the surface area of the shell.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        Surface area $\\,=4\\pi {\\int }_{0}^{1}$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $x^2\\sqrt{1+16x^2}$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\text{d}x.$\n\nEarlier part 4:\n\nWrite down the missing parts of a parametrization of our shell below.\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $r(x,\\theta )=⟨x,\\,2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,$ \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2x^2\\sin(\\theta)$                \n                                    \n                     