                    \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $Q={∬}_{S}^{}d(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        $2\\pi$                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        .\n\nCurrent part:\n\nFor the transformation $r:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{3},$ defined as\n\n$$\nr(x)=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}],\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ \\theta \\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\nthe total derivative ${r}^{′}$ is given by \n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & a \\\\ b & -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & c\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        $a+b+c=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387728 1113 #uuid "7570f300-bb31-54e2-a90b-186e439f087c" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387728 1145 "Suppose a transformation $f:{R}^{n}\\to {R}^{m}$ is defined by \n\n$$\nf:[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {x}_{n}\\end{aligned}]⟶[\\begin{aligned}{f}_{1}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ {f}_{2}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n}) \\\\ ⋮ \\\\ {f}_{m}({x}_{1},{x}_{2},…,{x}_{n})\\end{aligned}],\n$$\n\n \n\nwhere ${f}_{1},{f}_{2},…,{f}_{m}$ are scalar functions with $n$ variables. If $f$ is differentiable at $x,$ then the total derivative of $f$ at $x,$ denoted ${f}^{′}(x),$ is given by the $m\\times n$ matrix\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{1}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{2}}{∂{x}_{n}} \\\\ ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ & ⋮ \\\\ \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{1}} & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{2}} & ⋯ & \\frac{∂{f}_{m}}{∂{x}_{n}}\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIn our case, we have the following:\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂{r}_{1}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{r}_{1}}{∂\\theta } \\\\ \\frac{∂{r}_{2}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{r}_{2}}{∂\\theta } \\\\ \\frac{∂{r}_{3}}{∂x} & \\frac{∂{r}_{3}}{∂\\theta }\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}| & | \\\\ {r}_{x}^{′} & {r}_{\\theta }^{′} \\\\ | & |\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nWe computed the partial derivatives in part 5:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{x}^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂x}(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\,{r}_{\\theta }^{′}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(x) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ) \\\\ \\frac{∂}{∂\\theta }(2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n{r}^{′}(x)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & -2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4x\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & 2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a+b+c & =0+4x\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\  & =(2{x}^{2}+4x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387729 1000 #edb/ref 17592186387730 13194139536184 true] [17592186387729 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139536184 true] [17592186387729 1041 "field-1" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387729 1104 #edb/ref 17592186387730 13194139536184 true] [17592186387729 1110 #uuid "0546847e-0fd8-5af1-8d7e-e56d87b98df9" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387730 1034 "4x\\cos(\\theta)+2x^2\\cos(\\theta)" 13194139536184 true] [17592186387730 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536184 true] [17592186387730 1111 #uuid "d52b8bfc-215c-5a79-8f16-7b17b7d5860a" 13194139536184 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-167647" 17592186387708 "q-167647/field-1" 17592186387709 "q-167647/field-1/9475f7eaf857030c1d1c2cbc6f876721724942f74feaba5c389ce184fd0768a9" 17592186387710 "q-167647/field-2" 17592186387711 "q-167647/field-2/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" 17592186387712 "q-167648" 17592186387713 "q-167648/field-1" 17592186387714 "q-167648/field-1/af8728b6c6527e8e0419e3f8f8b8a0039ad0ce2aead87934407adf20d1826090" 17592186387715 "q-167649" 17592186387716 "q-167649/field-1" 17592186387717 "q-167649/field-1/f37b140e44c3c1469a0b674232c5aaeb4f71e6e7b8d79e0c213b062c66caacc7" 17592186387718 "q-167650" 17592186387719 "q-167650/field-1" 17592186387720 "q-167650/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" 17592186387721 "q-167651" 17592186387722 "q-167651/field-1" 17592186387723 "q-167651/field-1/11b0c12a88afa8877677b43b6786ef134a2f058c37104b68adb7327f5dfdaabe" 17592186387724 "q-167652" 17592186387725 "q-167652/field-1" 17592186387726 "q-167652/field-1/99f48c1b72e8eeab33eba2584ff0661456642ba13c82a72d98a76e8e1a07563e" 17592186387727 "q-167658" 17592186387728 "q-167658/field-1" 